1. **K15 bonds first; then session spine** (F3/4/5/9, A8, W17). K15 already owns the selected face atom and faceless-vessel rule; let it finish signing before session callers encode authority. Shared files: node/browser openers and CLI face choice, especially their identity hunks; session work takes the later open/call hunks. Red: two concurrent node sessions cross-read a receipt or copied socket, old generation signs, or wrong-face working address opens. Control: same-face later CLI reads its receipt; A and B run concurrently. Positive: selected atom signs each face operation, faceless vessel serves floor only. Hold `session-contract`, `session-face/signer`, UDS, verb VM, working-slot resolver, CLI `persona`, node opener. **Identity and genesis bytes move here through K15 and working-address genesis; finish before bake.** [K15 brief](/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/brief.md); [contract:190,259-263](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem).
2. **Scoped surfaces and holder** (F1/2/6, P13, B2). Red: arbitrary foreign document or catalog name leaks, two tabs share an island or reply, stale port paints, browser starts a second Repo. Control: same-face permitted bag and content read, two same-face tabs get distinct islands, failed boot retries. Positive: node and browser each resolve a recipe at mount, one holder owns Repo/daemon, asker seals, leaf sync obeys one-way gate. Hold pool/view/recipe, node/browser compose callers, holder, TW5 view port and kernel. **Heavy D2 overlap:** TW5 island/port, hand gate, projection sink, and the opener port-lease hunks; serialize final integration against D2's landed port interface. **K15 overlap:** opener face-supplier and sealer hunks; merge after its signer lands. No new identity bytes, but recipe and working binding affect founding shape [road:592-594](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem).
3. **Hands and attribution** (F11 remainder, F12, F10). Red: unleased file edits sign, stale watch generation commits, standing seat signs authority, spoofed `modifier` gains face attribution, silent fleet device acts before catch-up. Control: attended direct ask edits only named tiddlers; standing seat drafts; verified change labels its face; current fleet device acts. Positive: watcher leases a face wiki, MCP and CLI share refusals and receipts, Mask travels as a non-authorizing field. Hold watch/projector, MCP adapter, profile gate, parallel drafts, fleet UI/removal. D2 touches projector/projection sink; take its landed hand gate. K15 touches fleet signer and face removal only at API edges. **Authorship record format and fleet relation bytes merit pre-bake closure.** [contract:71-90](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem).
4. **Intent and effects** (G13; I2 after I1). Red: forged writer, duplicate after restart, wrong audience, relay alters argument, revoked agent grant admits. Control: fresh authorized intent executes once, independent audience slots answer, valid far agent reaches a face device. Positive: working-only tombstone, durable lease/fence and effect receipt; relay countersigns admission only. Hold dispatcher/summons, effect reader, intent-plane adapter and relay seat. K15 supplies atom verification; G15's after-roll chain supplies the causal fence; D2 shares no core file. **Intent log/receipt formats and relay grant bytes move before bake if genesis seeds them** [face-intent-plane.mem:45-52,86-92](/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem).

