/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:190:''A request's outcome rests with the face's proof subject and the digest of its input.'' A receipt bound to the session that asked would strand a one-shot CLI run, whose session ends with its process. So a ''newly verified session wearing the same face'' reads the receipt by request id, and a session wearing another face reads nothing. Cancel, unknown-outcome and no-silent-redispatch hold as they stand. An explicit vessel audit facet may read across faces; an ordinary session never inherits it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:238:''Tiers contract outward by signed, narrowed relations.'' One operator's household Nexus, neighbourhood Lararium, tribe and regional Nexus stand as distinct realms, charters and seats over one vessel or several. Carriage carries and reads nothing; a seat, a realm membership, a document read and a promotion each take their own grant, and no tier inherits another's membership or map by transit. Tiers sharing one origin, host or relay can correlate by metadata; where tiers must not learn of each other, they run on separate substrate. The research rests at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/browser-trust-line-2026">>.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:251:At every ending the session's facets, signer handles, dials, scoped views, routes and island leases drop.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:259:# ''Freeze and preflight.'' New calls on this session freeze. The owner preflights the target face's custody or delegation, admit, causal relation, absolute planes, proof subject and effective recipes, as immutable descriptions. It MUST NOT mount the target face before the old facets fall: one session would then hold two live face views. A refused preflight leaves the old generation live.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:261:# ''Fence the old generation.'' Its dials stop, its operation and signer facets fall, its scoped document channels close, and its surfaces and islands dispose. An effect in flight resolves through its durable receipt.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:262:# ''Advance, mount, dial.'' The generation advances. The target surfaces mount under the new scoped view, and the session dials with fresh keys under the target face's proof.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:263:# ''Write the outcome.'' A mount or a dial that fails at commit closes this session and reports the partial outcome; the caller opens afresh. Nothing restores the old face's authority in silence.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:288:* ''The face a session wears, and its signer'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/session-face.ts`, `session-signer.ts`, over `face-authority.ts` and `face-proof-subjects.ts`). One function joins a verified chain, this vessel's own key for the face, the admit's verdict and the PersonaGroup's private grant into the `face` value, and derives the proof subject and the four planes itself; a signer mints for one live session, asks the owner's table before every signature, and drops at a close or a switch.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:295:# ''The face proof and its grants.'' Two faces on one vessel present different proof subjects, and a copied id or an own-hand claim gains no plane (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The subjects, private authority, the session signer and the one face supplier stand specified in code. The debt closes when the node's session open on the local socket and the browser holder call the supplier and mint a signer at every open. Those callers wait on three things: the custody rows for the face proof key and each vessel's face-scoped key, an admit that signs what it carries, and the ring's lookup by face subject (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/owed">>). The supplier's face names one PersonaGroup at one Nexus; a face at two Nexuses waits on this contract's word.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:16:role              = "face-proof — how a session proves ONE face at a gate without naming its vessel, under the PER-VESSEL shape: the face proof key per (PersonaGroup, Nexus) stays with the root-holding vessel and no private face key travels; each joined vessel mints its own face-scoped key, certified once at the join; a session signer chains beneath it. The gate reads face key → vessel's face-scoped key → session key, under one Nexus admit per face. Carries the key hierarchy, the gate exchange (a minimal Noise IK first flight in the WebSocket subprotocol token, provisional work only, a signed finish before any verdict), what the gate, a herm, a co-member and an observer each learn, the named leaks, causal deny-only withdrawal, the sibling channel's move to face scope, and what an offline root holder means"
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:30:''Two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/the-session">>). A proof that names the vessel breaks that at the first gate two sessions both dial. So a session proves itself under a ''face-scoped proof subject'', and this carrier states how that subject's keys come into being, what a gate checks, and what each party along the way learns.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:32:''Why this stands as its own carrier, beside the session contract.'' The session contract (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">>) governs the inside of one vessel: its owner, its islands, its holder. This carrier governs the wire: a gate, a herm, a sibling and an observer read it, and none of them reads the holder's protocol. The two meet at one field, the session's proof subject, and each builds on its own order.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:45:| ''Face proof key'', one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus) | the root-holding vessel mints it at random, independent of every other key, and authorizes its public half in private causal face state | the root-holding vessel; ''its private half never travels'' | a gate sees the public half as the admitted `nym` |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:46:| ''A vessel's face-scoped key'', one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus, vessel) | the joined vessel mints it at random; the face key certifies it ONCE, at the join | that vessel's custody; its trusted daemon invokes it | a gate sees it and its certificate inside the encrypted exchange |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:47:| Session signer, one per (session, Nexus) | the vessel's daemon mints it; the vessel's face-scoped key certifies it for a dial | a session-bound handle; it drops when the session closes or switches | a gate sees its public half and its certificate inside the encrypted exchange |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:48:| Per-dial transport keys | the dialer mints fresh X25519 static and ephemeral pairs | one dial's memory | a gate sees the initiator's static after decryption; a passive observer sees the ephemeral |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:49:| Herm relay identity | the dialer mints a separate fresh signer for each herm dial | one dial's memory | the herm sees this key and a face-scoped channel tag |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:50:| Gate bundle | the gate derives separate, domain-separated transport and signing keys per (tier, Nexus, route): a floor route's from the floor key, a serving route's from the serving key, a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (#/the-gate-exchange) | nowhere: a bundle lives in memory from a derivation to a drop; a dialer pins it per (Nexus, route) | the dialer, and anyone handed the pin |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:52:''The face's lineage re-issues the face proof key.'' The standing key and a successor minted at random both sign one hand-over; the record rides the Nexus's carriage board, the admit keeps naming the key the Nexus admitted, and a gate reads that key's line, stands a presenter under its head alone, and reads a line that forks as denied. A kapae on any key of the line holds the whole line. A gate that has not yet read the hand-over still stands the key it handed on, and no shared moment closes that gap; a compromise of the key therefore takes the face-key roll (#/causal-withdrawal), never a hand-over. A Handle card names its handle-KEL prefix, which no per-Nexus key enters, so a hand-over moves no card (house reading).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:54:''A vessel's face-scoped key never derives from, and never equals, a vessel root.'' It stands independently random per (PersonaGroup, Nexus, vessel), so no key and no certificate field repeats across two faces of one vessel. The types forbid a vessel-root key and any cross-face field in a proof.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:56:''The signing face key never fills the transport's static slot.'' A fresh X25519 key per dial fills it; the Ed25519 face key signs and does nothing else.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:64:''`face key (the admitted nym)` → `the vessel's face-scoped key` → `session key`.'' The Nexus quorum admits the FACE key once per Nexus. A vessel's certificate stands as a delegate beneath that admitted face; it takes no Nexus admit of its own.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:66:''The admit proves Nexus standing; the private face grant proves PersonaGroup capability. Neither substitutes for the other.'' A gate outside the PersonaGroup needs the Nexus admit alone. A gate that shares PersonaGroup planes also asks the ring to verify the private, root-authorized grant against that face's event history. No root edge rides beside the leaf (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/two-maps">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:76:The dialer pins the gate bundle before it dials. Every signature uses its own domain bytes and a canonical field encoding.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:78:# ''The first flight.'' A browser's upgrade request carries the knock in its URL path and a ''minimal'' Noise IK message 1 as a token in `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol`, beside one fixed application protocol name. A node dialer rides the same upgrade, knock path and subprotocol token through its `ws` client (`nodeDialSocket` over `wsDialSocket`): one upgrade on both hosts.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:79:# ''The gate answers the upgrade only after that flight decrypts.'' A flight that decrypts shows the dialer knows the gate's pinned key, which silence toward strangers protects. The gate then sends its 101 and selects the fixed protocol name alone. A wrong knock or a flight that fails to decrypt draws no answer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:84:''The admit's signed bytes carry the canon-document list and a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at its named Nexus. `readGateBundlePin` reads the object and its digest derives from it; the quorum's salted `carriageCommit` binds the opening inside the act image. A joinee reads the opening only through the admit at its held root (`verifySignedAdmitBundle`). Floor routes receive separate full pins through an authenticated relation or signed pin set; a floor announcement cannot authenticate its own first pin. `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge, and the fleet answer carries the pin and canon list.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:87:# ''The signed finish.'' The session signer signs the COMPLETED handshake hash, the gate bundle's digest, the face key, the presentation, the audience and the session key. A recorder of the first flight lacks the dial's secrets and cannot produce it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:89:# ''Both ends close the dial'' and discard its transport and herm-dial keys. The daemon drops the session signer when its session ends or switches.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:93:> ''House readings, marked as such; the operator may overturn each.'' The gate and the dialer that stand specified in code (#/owed) read the exchange above this way.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:95:* ''The knock derives from the bundle's digest'', and the handshake's prologue holds that digest. So a gate's knock, its pin, its verdict and its posture all read per Nexus exactly, and a first flight decrypts only at the gate whose pin its dialer held.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:97:* ''No collaborator hears of a dial before its finish verifies.'' The admit reader, the rings, the sorter and the gate's memory act on no first flight.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:101:* ''An OPEN gate answers a stranger.'' A sound chain under a face no quorum admitted, presenting no arm, sorts as a stranger where this Nexus reads OPEN: the gate answers `verified`, seats it at the public shelf and keeps nothing of that face's history. Where the Nexus reads PRIVATE the same presenter draws silence. The four states that refuse (`unconfirmed`, `withdrawn`, `incomplete`, `forked`) go to a presenter of an admitted face alone.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:102:* ''The session table takes the session before the verdict leaves, and opens it after.'' A dialer never holds a verdict for a session the gate did not seat.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:104:* ''A dial draws a deadline of its own.'' A gate that answers a flight and then waits forever holds no dial open.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:105:* ''Whether a hosting grant or an invite claim holds stays the sorter's own reading.'' The gate binds the arm to the face key and the Nexus, and attaches a walker only where the sorter read one.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:106:* ''One presentation rides one dial.'' A presenter that reads `unconfirmed` or `incomplete` folds what it received and dials again.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:107:* ''A dialer carries its whole line unless its caller names less'', so the first honest vessel of a face ends a gate's partition in one dial.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:114:''A route names its tier, and a tier names its root.'' A ''floor route'' answers at a locked vessel: the public shelf, the oracle's read face, the floor's announcement, and a herm's blind relay of bytes it cannot open. Its bundle derives from the floor key. A ''sovereign route'' seats a face's session, syncs a private document or serves a lane whose bytes this vessel can open. Its bundle derives from the sealed custody root, and it exists only while the vessel stands unlocked. A route's typed name carries its tier, the pin states it and the pin's digest binds it: no route asks the other tier's root, a root asked for the wrong tier refuses by name, and a dialer that pinned one tier believes no gate of the other.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:116:''Each derivation takes the tier, the Nexus and the route under its own name.'' No pin, key, digest or knock of one tier, one Nexus or one route links to another for an outsider: one vessel's floor pin and its sovereign pin for one Nexus share nothing.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:118:''A dialer names the tier it means to reach'', and a pin of another tier dials nothing: a floor gate's `verified` seats the floor alone, so no caller mistakes it for a sovereign seat.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:122:''A floor gate seats no fleet lane.'' It asks no private grant and sorts nobody same-operator, it reads no withdrawal memory and answers no refusing state, and it marks every seat it opens as the floor's, so that seat reaches the public shelf and what the floor serves, and nothing this vessel can open. A presenter that asks more dials the sovereign route, and finds no gate there while the vessel rests locked. A floor route a design adds keeps this law: the ember's route (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-raise">>) seats a dialer by the transport key a standing ember pin names, and no device of the person's fleet by its fleet key.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:128:''A serving route answers at a vessel its embers raised to SERVING'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>): the serving gate for presenters already standing, and blind carriage for them. Its bundle derives from the serving key under its own registered domain, and it exists only while the vessel stands at SERVING or unlocked. The floor and sovereign tiers stand untouched: no serving route asks the floor key or the custody root, and a dialer that pinned the sovereign tier believes no serving gate. A serving gate signs its own handshake and no act, and its seat reaches what the serving tier holds and nothing beyond it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:136:''A herm or a carrier holds no face'', so it holds no face key, no certificate and no session certificate. It still dials gates. The presentation therefore takes a fourth arm, the ''place arm'', and that arm stands OUTSIDE the face proof: no chain rides it and no withdrawal history answers it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:139:* ''It presents the contract that names that key and this gate's Nexus'': the quorum's `carry` act with the place's own carrier seal. The gate reads it through the same held-root door an admit passes, against the board's counted `uncarry` acts and the antigen, and consults the edge shadow ring for the carriage edge.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:142:* ''A standing names the presenter's own key.'' Where the sorter names a standing, for a place or for a face, it stands under the key that proved in this dial and at this gate's Nexus, or the dial draws silence.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:144:* ''One arm rides one dial.'' A presentation that carries a place arm beside a certificate, or a face's arm with no chain, reads as none.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:145:* ''A place with no contract'' that dials a floor route draws what a proven stranger draws there.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:149:▢ ''OWED'': an operator's contract over their own herm (one signature, one place, one Nexus) names bytes no code holds yet; the arm reads the quorum's `carry` act until it does.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:157:''A browser offers two protocols, in this order'': the fixed name `lar-gate`, then Noise IK message one as ONE unpadded base64url token. A minimal flight weighs 96 bytes and spells 128 characters, so the header value weighs 138 bytes and one flight spells one way. A flight that carries a payload never leaves the dialer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:159:''The gate's 101 selects `lar-gate` alone'' and never echoes the token. The browser dialer reads the protocol its socket opened under and cuts any other: Chromium fails a 101 that selects nothing, while Firefox and WebKit open it under the protocol `""`, so only the dialer's own check holds the line in every engine. A foreign selection fails in all three.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:183:| The Nexus gate | the stable face key AT THAT NEXUS, so it correlates that face's sessions there (ruled acceptable: two sessions of one face may correlate); the presenting vessel's face-scoped key; the session key; the presentation and its lineage; route and audience | a vessel root key, a persona root, a root edge, or the number of vessels a face holds |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:184:| A herm | a per-dial relay key, a face-scoped channel tag, routing, locators, timing, sizes and destination; a stable tag lets it correlate ONE face's carriage | the sibling proof, document content, any certificate in the chain, or a tag two faces share |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:196:* ''A withdrawal history's length tells each gate the face dials how many keys that face has withdrawn there.'' A gate that never met a withdrawn vessel learns the count and nothing of the key.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:200:* ''A household TLS terminator, its log's reader, or a herm that sees the upgrade, once it holds candidate sovereign gate pins, learns which Nexus a dial selects among the K gates sharing its address and route (at most log2(K) bits per dial, none where K=1) and links that Nexus's repeat visits; the knock never tells it the presenting face, the admission verdict or any sealed byte.'' The operator's ruling of 2026-10-26 places this reader outside the sovereign route's promise. A sovereign pin escaping its members' custody, or a ruling that extends route confidentiality to pin-holders, reopens `W10` (the reading and its measurements stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:210:* ''Removing one vessel withdraws ONE certificate.'' The face key signs a causal withdrawal into a ''deny-only withdrawal history'' (#/the-withdrawal-proof). A gate checks a presented chain against the withdrawals it has learned. It never consults a positive list of current vessels, and it never asks an online service whether a key still belongs. The PersonaGroup's own membership withdrawal, its rekey and the re-sealing of standing content run beside it. No face-key roll and no fresh Nexus admit follows from one vessel's removal.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:213:* ''A face-key roll'' answers a compromise of the root-held face key itself: a private causal authorization, then the affected Nexus boards' revoke and admit. No clock lapses either relation.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:223:''The face key alone authors the history.'' One history stands per face key, so one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus). Each event carries the face key, the Nexus, its position, the head of the event before it, and a digest of the withdrawn vessel's face-scoped key. The face key signs it under the withdrawal's own domain. The first event names a genesis head derived from the face key and the Nexus. No quorum signs and no board carries the history: the Nexus admitted the face key once, and a vessel's certificate stands as a delegate beneath it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:225:''A denial names a key by digest.'' The digest binds the face key and the Nexus, so a gate that never met the vessel learns nothing of its key, and no two histories share a value. The denial covers every certificate the face key ever signs for that key. Every denial the face key signed counts wherever a reader verified it, whether or not the reader holds the events before it. ''A withdrawn key never returns'': a vessel that joins again mints a fresh key and takes a fresh certificate (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/re-admission">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:229:''The history travels with the face's own presenters, and with nobody else.'' Each vessel of the face brings the history to every gate it dials. A gate keeps the events of the faces that presented to it. It hands them to a presenter whose chain verified under that same face key, and to no other party: no board, no shelf and no other gate receives them from it. The gate keeps denials and never the certificates it saw, so it holds no inventory of a face's vessels (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/registry-filter#/the-test">>).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:258:* ''One row per face key'', named by the digest that binds that face key to this Nexus, and at most 1024 events in it; a 1025th refuses. The gate reads one row for one presenter and never walks the rows. One writer moves a row at a time, and one vessel holds its store, so no two keeps lose each other's event.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:262:* ''A fresh vessel knows nothing'', and accepts as a gate that learned nothing accepts (#/named-leaks), until the first honest vessel of a face dials it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:268:| a gate that learned nothing newer, facing the withdrawn vessel | that gate accepts the withdrawn vessel under the admitted face | the first honest vessel of that face to dial the gate; nothing else in this proof |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:275:''A withheld withdrawal buys a delay and never a lift.'' The delay lasts at each gate until an honest vessel of the face dials it. The PersonaGroup's own rekey closes the private planes beside this proof and waits on no gate.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:279:''Two acts remove a vessel, and each answers to its own readers.'' The dyad marker sets a device aside inside its fleet: it rides the fleet's edge board, closes the sibling lane and device sync, and moves the PersonaGroup's keys (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). The certificate withdrawal denies that vessel's face-scoped key at one Nexus's gates, and rides the face's own presentations. One removal signs the dyad raise once, and one withdrawal for each face key the vessel held a certificate under. The root-holding vessel signs both, each with one signature.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:281:* ''Neither act rides a Nexus board.'' A gate reads the withdrawal and never the dyad; a sibling reads both.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:291:''A session's certificate names its hand's profile, and the profile bounds the key.'' A session key signs under three purposes, each with its own domain: the dial's signed finish, an ordinary act, and an act that changes who holds authority. A person's tab and a person's CLI run sign all three. The disk watcher and a spirit's seat sign the first two, and no verifier reads an authority act under their key (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>). The watcher's row reads as the house's own: the ruling names the seat.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:297:''A session's face names one PersonaGroup at ONE Nexus'' (house reading). The proof subject and the admit both stand per Nexus, and the session contract's face carries one of each. A face that works at two Nexuses holds one signer for each (#/the-key-hierarchy); whether one session carries both or two sessions carry one each stays the session contract's word to give.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:316:''The sibling-facing proof moves to face scope together with the herm-facing stamp.'' The channel seals a face-scoped session proof and the face-private membership authority to its sibling, and binds its Repo peer id to the proven face session. It transmits no device delegation and derives no peer id from a device key. The herm stamps the separate per-dial relay identity alone.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:330:* a joined vessel keeps using the certificate it holds, under the face key the Nexus already admitted;
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:350:* ''The gate bundle'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`): the floor and sovereign tiers with their typed routes and roots (the serving tier stands owed with the ember's train E), the pin, its digest, the knock, the prologue, and the transport and signing keys one gate derives per (tier, Nexus, route). Nothing rests. Its caller: the vessel's gate composer.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:351:* ''The exchange's subjects'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-exchange.ts`): the presentation and the answer with their readers, the image of the finish, the image of the verdict, the browser's first-flight envelope with its reader and its refusals (#/the-browser-envelope), and the house's sealed frame layout, frozen: tags `0x01` to `0x0f` carry dialer frames, `0x11` to `0x1f` gate frames, a later frame takes an unassigned tag in its direction's block and moves none, and every byte outside the table reads reserved (`GATE_FRAME`, `gateFrameTagReserved`, `gateFrameTableRefusal`; the lane kit `docs/pono/w28-gate-lane` carries the table).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:353:* ''The dialers'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-dial.ts`): the other half of the exchange, for a face and for a faceless place, one function each for a node and a browser. Their callers: both client transports, at the cutover.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:359:* ''Two custody rows.'' The face proof key rests cold with the root holder, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus); a vessel's face-scoped key rests hot on its own vessel, one per (PersonaGroup, Nexus). Each holds 32 secret bytes and reads whole or refuses by name. The modules name the rows and the two signing doors they ask of the custody seat, and write no row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:361:* ''The private grant's reader.'' The record that binds a face key to its PersonaGroup at one Nexus rests in the group's private causal state, and the ring reads it by vessel key today.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:365:* ''A held Nexus root per gate'': the roster, the charter lineage, the deny board and the antigen that the admit reader folds, with the causal position it read them at. A gate that holds no root refuses every admit by name.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:367:* ''The sorter over proven facts'': a class from a held admit, a private grant, the fleet reading and the arm as presented, over ONE Nexus's posture.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:373:* ''The withdrawal proof under a live partition.'' The fold and the six verdicts stand proven as pure functions over synthetic histories, and the six answers stand proven at one gate against a dialer in the same process, partitioned by hand. No two gates and no real herm have yet carried one.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:380:# ''The gate, behind interfaces.'' Specified in code, with the bundle's root, the held Nexus root, the rings by face key and the sorter over proven facts owed.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:381:# ''One wire cutover.'' Node and browser dialers, gate, sorter and ring lookup move together, and the vessel-key proof paths retire in the same step.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:382:# ''Sibling carriage.'' The herm dial, the inner proof and the sibling peer id move to face scope.

